{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8f246224-6e43-44c4-8b97-7390d17942c8",
    "name": "Webbeet UX Audit Tool",
    "description": "API for the Webbeet UX Audit Tool. One endpoint: `POST /api/audit`.\n\nThe response is **Server-Sent Events** (`text/event-stream`), not plain JSON. Two events stream back:\n- `partial` — Phase 1, fast (~3-5s): SEO, Trust, UX checks from the HTML (29 checks)\n- `complete` — Phase 2, slow (~15-90s): Performance, Mobile, Accessibility from PageSpeed + Puppeteer (22 checks)\n\nError responses (400 / 422 / 429) are plain JSON and fire before the stream starts.\n\n⚠️ **Set Postman request timeout to 120 000 ms** (Settings → General → Request timeout) or heavy sites will cut off early.\n\n**Score bands:** 80-100 Good · 50-79 Needs work · 0-49 Poor\n**Check statuses:** `pass` · `warning` · `fail`",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Switch to https://ux-audit.exlinelabs.co.uk for production"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Happy Path",
      "description": "Successful audit requests. Responses are SSE — the test scripts parse the `data:` lines and assert on both phases.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Audit - webbeet.studio",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Parse SSE: split on newlines, pick up 'data: {...}' lines",
                  "const events = pm.response.text().split('\\n')",
                  "    .filter(l => l.startsWith('data: '))",
                  "    .map(l => { try { return JSON.parse(l.slice(6)); } catch(e) { return null; } })",
                  "    .filter(Boolean);",
                  "",
                  "const partial  = events.find(e => e.type === 'partial');",
                  "const complete = events.find(e => e.type === 'complete');",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 OK with event-stream content type', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('text/event-stream');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Phase 1 — partial event received (seo / trust / ux)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(partial).to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "    ['seo','trust','ux'].forEach(c => pm.expect(partial.categories).to.have.property(c));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Phase 1 — 29 checks returned', () => {",
                  "    const n = Object.values(partial?.categories ?? {}).reduce((s,c) => s + (c.checks?.length ?? 0), 0);",
                  "    pm.expect(n).to.equal(29);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Phase 2 — complete event received (performance / mobile / accessibility)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(complete).to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "    ['performance','mobile','accessibility'].forEach(c => pm.expect(complete.categories).to.have.property(c));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Phase 2 — overallScore is 0-100', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(complete?.overallScore).to.be.a('number').and.within(0, 100);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Phase 2 — shareId returned (Supabase connected)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(complete?.shareId).to.be.a('string').and.have.length.above(0);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('All checks have required fields and valid status', () => {",
                  "    const allCats = Object.assign({}, partial?.categories, complete?.categories);",
                  "    Object.values(allCats).forEach(cat => {",
                  "        (cat.checks ?? []).forEach(c => {",
                  "            pm.expect(c).to.include.all.keys('id','label','value','status','description');",
                  "            pm.expect(['pass','warning','fail']).to.include(c.status);",
                  "        });",
                  "    });",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Console summary",
                  "if (complete) {",
                  "    console.log('Overall:', complete.overallScore);",
                  "    Object.entries(Object.assign({}, partial?.categories, complete?.categories)).forEach(([k,v]) => {",
                  "        console.log(' ' + k + ':', v.unavailable ? 'unavailable' : v.score + ' (' + (v.checks?.length ?? 0) + ' checks)');",
                  "    });",
                  "    console.log('shareId:', complete.shareId ?? 'none');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"https://webbeet.studio\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Primary benchmark — audits the Webbeet homepage across all 6 categories (51 checks total). Expect a `partial` event within ~5s (SEO/Trust/UX) followed by a `complete` event within ~20s (Performance/Mobile/Accessibility) once PageSpeed finishes.\n\nCheck the **Console** tab in Test Results for a readable score breakdown."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Audit - HTTP site (HTTPS flag)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const events = pm.response.text().split('\\n')",
                  "    .filter(l => l.startsWith('data: '))",
                  "    .map(l => { try { return JSON.parse(l.slice(6)); } catch(e) { return null; } })",
                  "    .filter(Boolean);",
                  "const partial = events.find(e => e.type === 'partial');",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Trust > https check is fail for http:// URLs', () => {",
                  "    const httpsCheck = (partial?.categories?.trust?.checks ?? []).find(c => c.id === 'https');",
                  "    pm.expect(httpsCheck, 'https check missing from trust category').to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "    pm.expect(httpsCheck.status).to.equal('fail');",
                  "    pm.expect(httpsCheck.value).to.include('Not secure');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"http://neverssl.com\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Audits `neverssl.com` — a real site intentionally kept on HTTP with no redirect. Verifies that the Trust category's `https` check correctly returns `status: 'fail'` and `value: 'Not secure (http)'` for non-HTTPS URLs."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Error Cases",
      "description": "All failure modes. These errors fire **before** the stream opens so responses are plain JSON, not SSE.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Missing URL field",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Error message mentions https://', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.include('https');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Sends an empty body with no `url` field. Expected response: `400` with `\"Please enter a valid website URL including https://\"`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "URL without https:// protocol",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Error message mentions https://', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.include('https');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"webbeet.studio\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Sends a bare domain with no `https://` prefix. Expected response: `400` with `\"Please enter a valid website URL including https://\"`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Unreachable domain",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422 Unprocessable Entity', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test('Error says we could not reach the URL', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.include(\"couldn't reach\");",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"https://this-domain-does-not-exist-xyz99abc.io\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Sends a syntactically valid URL that does not resolve. The reachability HEAD check fails and the API returns `422` with `\"We couldn't reach that URL. Check it's live and try again.\"`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Invalid JSON body",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Error says Invalid request body', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.include('Invalid');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "this is not json",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Sends malformed JSON in the request body. Expected response: `400` with `\"Invalid request body.\"`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Wrong method (GET)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('405 Method Not Allowed', () => pm.response.to.have.status(405));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "The `/api/audit` endpoint only accepts `POST`. Sending `GET` returns `405 Method Not Allowed` — handled automatically by Next.js App Router."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Rate Limiting",
      "description": "25 audits per IP per hour. The 26th request returns 429 before the stream opens — response is plain JSON.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Trigger rate limit (send 6 times)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const status = pm.response.code;",
                  "pm.test('400 (under limit) or 429 (rate limited)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect([400, 429]).to.include(status);",
                  "});",
                  "if (status === 429) {",
                  "    pm.test('429 message mentions an hour', () => {",
                  "        pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.include('hour');",
                  "    });",
                  "    console.log('Rate limit hit — working correctly');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('Under limit — send again to reach 25 (then 429 on the 26th)');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"not-a-url\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Send this request **26 times in a row**. Sends an invalid URL so no PageSpeed quota is burned. Runs 1-25 return `400`. Run 26 returns `429` with `\"You've run several audits recently. Try again in an hour.\"`\n\nTo reset the counter: restart the dev server (the limiter is in-memory)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
